Think: Create the script file peak_login_task/count_peak_logins.sh with a single-command awk implementation (comments allowed) that parses timestamps, writes extracted/invalid/peak files, writes peak_count.txt, and prints the integer.

Act: bash

```bash
cat > peak_login_task/count_peak_logins.sh <<'EOF'
#!/bin/sh
# count_peak_logins.sh
# Description: Counts logins between 21:00 and 23:59 (inclusive) from server.log located in the same directory.
# Input (placeholder): server.log
# Output (placeholder): peak_count.txt
# Additional outputs: extracted_times.txt (all valid extracted timestamps), invalid_entries.log (lines that do not match expected timestamp format), peak_times.txt (timestamps in the 21:00-23:59 range)
# Usage: run this script from the workspace directory: ./count_peak_logins.sh

awk '{
  # Attempt to extract a timestamp at the start of the line: one-or-two-digit hour, colon, two-digit minute (00-59)
  if (match($0, /^([0-9]{1,2}):([0-5][0-9])/, a)) {
    h = a[1] + 0;
    m = a[2] + 0;
    # Sanity check for hour range 0-23
    if (h >= 0 && h <= 23) {
      ts = sprintf("%02d:%02d", h, m);
      print ts >> "extracted_times.txt";
      # Check for peak window 21:00 - 23:59 inclusive
      if (h >= 21 && h <= 23) {
        print ts >> "peak_times.txt";
        peak++;
      }
    } else {
      print $0 >> "invalid_entries.log";
    }
  } else {
    print $0 >> "invalid_entries.log";
  }
}
END {
  if (peak == "" ) peak = 0;
  # Write only the integer count to peak_count.txt and also print the integer to stdout
  print peak > "peak_count.txt";
  print peak;
}' server.log
EOF
```

Think: Validate each raw value by checking temp_workspace/raw_values/<filename> matches an integer regex; write any invalid entries as "filename:content" (or ":<missing>" if unreadable) to temp_workspace/invalid.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  fname="temp_workspace/raw_values/" $0;
  content="";
  if ((getline content < fname) > 0) {
    gsub(/\r/,"",content);
    if (content !~ /^[+-]?[0-9]+$/) print $0 ":" content
  } else {
    print $0 ":<missing>"
  }
  close(fname)
}' temp_workspace/file_list.txt > temp_workspace/invalid.txt
